From c5dc2fa1024d1231f20e99f70592ee25fbe464f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:11:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] ui: add the Zeo corner-radius token scale

Adds ZeoRadius -- the steps 0/2/4/6/8/12/16/full -- resolved through &App.
Zed's radius usage is bimodal (rounded_sm x30, rounded_md x30) with no token at
all; this gives corner radius the same settings-resolved treatment spacing
already has.

px() mirrors DynamicSpacing exactly: the 16px rem base lives only inside the
ratio, and the result multiplies by the live ui_font_size -- never by a
hard-coded 16. An implementation that pins the base compiles and passes every
other assertion, then silently drifts away from spacing the moment a user
changes ui_font_size.

Unlike DynamicSpacing there is no density triple: density governs the air
between elements, not the shape of one, so a 6px button stays 6px at
Comfortable. `Full` is a fixed sentinel -- a pill is a shape declaration, not a
measurement -- and is exempt from both ui_font_size and radius_scale.

The two new dev-dependencies are workspace-internal (settings, theme_settings);
the tests drive the real provider rather than a fake, so the token cannot pass
while the settings spine is broken. No new external crate.

Covers R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4, R1.7, R1.8.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
